<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>

<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Strategist Intelligence Hub</title>

<style>

*{
margin:0;
padding:0;
box-sizing:border-box;
}

body{

background:#0F1115;

font-family:
Inter,
system-ui,
-apple-system,
Arial,
sans-serif;

color:#E0E0E0;

line-height:1.6;

padding:30px 15px;

}

.container{

max-width:1200px;

margin:auto;

background:#1A1D23;

border-radius:28px;

padding:40px;

box-shadow:
0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.5);

border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.05);

}


/* =========================
HEADER
========================= */

header{

margin-bottom:35px;

}

h1{

font-size:2.6rem;

font-weight:800;

color:#FFFFFF;

letter-spacing:-1px;

margin-bottom:8px;

}

.subtitle{

color:#888;

margin-bottom:25px;

}


/* =========================
SIGNAL BAR
========================= */

.network-gate{

background:
rgba(197,160,89,.1);

color:#C5A059;

padding:18px;

border-radius:16px;

font-size:.82rem;

border:
1px solid rgba(197,160,89,.3);

margin-bottom:30px;

}


/* =========================
INTELLIGENCE CONTROL
========================= */

.control-panel{

display:grid;

grid-template-columns:
1fr 1fr;

gap:15px;

margin-bottom:35px;

}

.control-box{

background:#242830;

padding:18px;

border-radius:14px;

border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);

}

.control-box label{

display:block;

font-size:.7rem;

text-transform:uppercase;

letter-spacing:1px;

color:#C5A059;

font-weight:800;

margin-bottom:8px;

}

select{

width:100%;

padding:12px;

background:#15181d;

border:
1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);

border-radius:10px;

color:white;

font-size:.9rem;

}


/* =========================
GRID
========================= */

.intelligence-grid{

display:grid;

grid-template-columns:
repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));

gap:22px;

}


/* =========================
CARDS
========================= */

.opportunity-card{

background:#242830;

border-radius:20px;

padding:25px;

border:
1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.04);

transition:.3s;

}

.opportunity-card:hover{

transform:translateY(-5px);

border-color:
rgba(197,160,89,.35);

background:#292e36;

box-shadow:
0 15px 35px rgba(0,0,0,.3);

}


.strategy-badge{

font-size:.65rem;

font-weight:900;

text-transform:uppercase;

letter-spacing:1.5px;

color:#C5A059;

margin-bottom:10px;

display:block;

}

h2{

font-size:1.25rem;

margin-bottom:10px;

color:#FFF;

}

.opportunity-card > p{

color:#A0A0A0;

font-size:.92rem;

margin-bottom:18px;

}


/* =========================
EXPANDABLE INTELLIGENCE
========================= */

details{

border-top:
1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);

padding-top:15px;

}

summary{

cursor:pointer;

color:#C5A059;

font-weight:700;

font-size:.85rem;

list-style:none;

}

summary::-webkit-details-marker{

display:none;

}

summary::after{

content:"+";

float:right;

font-size:1.2rem;

}

details[open] summary::after{

content:"−";

}

.insight{

padding-top:15px;

color:#AAA;

font-size:.85rem;

}

.insight strong{

color:#E2BC75;

}


/* =========================
STRATEGIC MODEL
========================= */

.model{

margin-top:35px;

background:
linear-gradient(
135deg,
rgba(197,160,89,.12),
rgba(197,160,89,.03)
);

border:
1px solid rgba(197,160,89,.25);

border-radius:20px;

padding:30px;

}

.model h2{

color:#C5A059;

margin-bottom:10px;

}

.model-intro{

color:#999;

font-size:.9rem;

margin-bottom:25px;

}

.model-grid{

display:grid;

grid-template-columns:
repeat(auto-fit,minmax(160px,1fr));

gap:12px;

}

.model-step{

background:#20242a;

padding:18px;

border-radius:12px;

text-align:center;

}

.model-step span{

display:block;

font-size:.7rem;

color:#C5A059;

font-weight:800;

margin-bottom:5px;

}

.model-step strong{

color:white;

font-size:.9rem;

}


/* =========================
DECISION CHECK
========================= */

.decision{

margin-top:25px;

background:#20242a;

border-radius:18px;

padding:25px;

}

.decision h3{

color:#FFF;

margin-bottom:15px;

}

.decision-list{

display:grid;

grid-template-columns:
repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));

gap:10px;

}

.decision-item{

padding:15px;

background:#181b20;

border-radius:10px;

font-size:.82rem;

color:#AAA;

}

.decision-item strong{

display:block;

color:#C5A059;

margin-bottom:4px;

}


/* =========================
MOBILE
========================= */

@media(max-width:700px){

body{

padding:10px;

}

.container{

padding:25px 18px;

border-radius:20px;

}

h1{

font-size:2rem;

}

.control-panel{

grid-template-columns:1fr;

}

.intelligence-grid{

grid-template-columns:1fr;

}

}

</style>

</head>


<body>


<div class="container">


<header>


<div class="network-gate">

🛡️ <strong>STRATEGIC SIGNAL:</strong>
Focus on high-leverage information rather than information volume.

</div>


<h1>
Strategic Command
</h1>


<p class="subtitle">

Insight, opportunity, and the architecture of better decisions.

</p>


<!-- =========================
CONTROL PANEL
========================= -->

<div class="control-panel">


<div class="control-box">

<label for="focus">

Choose Intelligence Focus

</label>

<select id="focus">

<option>
All Strategic Areas
</option>

<option>
Technology
</option>

<option>
Career
</option>

<option>
Innovation
</option>

<option>
Business
</option>

<option>
Personal Strategy
</option>

</select>

</div>


<div class="control-box">

<label for="question">

Choose Your Strategic Question

</label>

<select id="question">

<option>
What should I investigate?
</option>

<option>
Where is leverage?
</option>

<option>
What am I overlooking?
</option>

<option>
What could become obsolete?
</option>

<option>
What can I build?
</option>

<option>
What should I stop doing?
</option>

</select>

</div>


</div>

</header>



<!-- =========================
INTELLIGENCE CARDS
========================= -->

<div class="intelligence-grid">


<!-- 1 -->

<article class="opportunity-card">

<span class="strategy-badge">
Technology Leverage
</span>

<h2>
AI-Agent Labor Force
</h2>

<p>

Administrative work is increasingly becoming
automatable. The strategic question is not simply
whether AI can do the work, but which workflows
should be redesigned around it.

</p>


<details>

<summary>
Open Strategic Analysis
</summary>

<div class="insight">

<strong>Look for:</strong>

repetitive tasks, predictable decisions,
data movement, scheduling, reporting,
customer communication, and internal workflows.

<br><br>

<strong>Strategic question:</strong>

If a task happens repeatedly and follows
recognizable rules, could the process be
redesigned rather than simply performed faster?

</div>

</details>

</article>



<!-- 2 -->

<article class="opportunity-card">

<span class="strategy-badge">
Innovation
</span>

<h2>
Cross-Industry Synthesis
</h2>

<p>

Some of the strongest ideas come from combining
methods that normally exist in different industries.

</p>


<details>

<summary>
Open Strategic Analysis
</summary>

<div class="insight">

<strong>Method:</strong>

Choose one industry with an interesting system.

Then ask:

"What would happen if this principle were
applied somewhere completely different?"

<br><br>

<strong>Example:</strong>

Apply logistics optimization to personal
productivity, or apply subscription economics
to professional services.

</div>

</details>

</article>



<!-- 3 -->

<article class="opportunity-card">

<span class="strategy-badge">
Personal Strategy
</span>

<h2>
The Phoenix Framework
</h2>

<p>

When a path stops producing useful results,
continuing harder may be less intelligent than
redesigning the path.

</p>


<details>

<summary>
Open Strategic Analysis
</summary>

<div class="insight">

<strong>Step 1:</strong>
Identify what is no longer working.

<br><br>

<strong>Step 2:</strong>
Separate sunk costs from future value.

<br><br>

<strong>Step 3:</strong>
Identify transferable skills and assets.

<br><br>

<strong>Step 4:</strong>
Test a new direction before making a full commitment.

</div>

</details>

</article>



<!-- 4 -->

<article class="opportunity-card">

<span class="strategy-badge">
Business Strategy
</span>

<h2>
Micro-SaaS Acquisition Thinking
</h2>

<p>

You do not always have to create an asset from
zero. Existing small businesses can reveal
opportunities to improve, acquire, automate,
or combine existing systems.

</p>


<details>

<summary>
Open Strategic Analysis
</summary>

<div class="insight">

<strong>Investigate:</strong>

Recurring revenue, customer retention,
operating costs, owner dependence,
automation opportunities, and neglected
distribution channels.

<br><br>

<strong>Key question:</strong>

Can an existing system become significantly
more valuable through better operations?

</div>

</details>

</article>



<!-- 5 -->

<article class="opportunity-card">

<span class="strategy-badge">
Career Intelligence
</span>

<h2>
Skill-to-Evidence Strategy
</h2>

<p>

Learning something is different from proving
you can use it. Career advancement becomes
stronger when skills produce visible evidence.

</p>


<details>

<summary>
Open Strategic Analysis
</summary>

<div class="insight">

<strong>Build the chain:</strong>

Learn → Practice → Build → Document → Demonstrate.

<br><br>

Instead of collecting credentials indefinitely,
create projects, analyses, case studies,
process improvements, portfolios, or measurable
work samples.

<br><br>

<strong>Goal:</strong>

Make your ability easier for another person
to evaluate.

</div>

</details>

</article>



<!-- 6 -->

<article class="opportunity-card">

<span class="strategy-badge">
Decision Intelligence
</span>

<h2>
The Leverage Point Audit
</h2>

<p>

Not every problem deserves equal effort.
The highest-value move is often finding the
small change that influences many downstream
results.

</p>


<details>

<summary>
Open Strategic Analysis
</summary>

<div class="insight">

<strong>Ask:</strong>

What repeatedly creates this problem?

What decision controls the most consequences?

What bottleneck limits everything else?

What action could improve several outcomes
simultaneously?

<br><br>

<strong>Principle:</strong>

Do not automatically work harder on the visible
problem. Investigate the system producing it.

</div>

</details>

</article>


</div>



<!-- =========================
STRATEGIC OPERATING MODEL
========================= -->

<section class="model">

<h2>
The Strategic Operating Model
</h2>

<p class="model-intro">

Use this six-stage process whenever you encounter
a major opportunity, problem, career decision,
business idea, or emerging technology.

</p>


<div class="model-grid">


<div class="model-step">

<span>01</span>

<strong>
Observe
</strong>

</div>


<div class="model-step">

<span>02</span>

<strong>
Question
</strong>

</div>


<div class="model-step">

<span>03</span>

<strong>
Map
</strong>

</div>


<div class="model-step">

<span>04</span>

<strong>
Test
</strong>

</div>


<div class="model-step">

<span>05</span>

<strong>
Measure
</strong>

</div>


<div class="model-step">

<span>06</span>

<strong>
Adapt
</strong>

</div>


</div>


<div class="decision">

<h3>
Before Making a Major Move, Ask:
</h3>


<div class="decision-list">


<div class="decision-item">

<strong>Leverage</strong>

What small action could create a large effect?

</div>


<div class="decision-item">

<strong>Evidence</strong>

What do I actually know versus assume?

</div>


<div class="decision-item">

<strong>Downside</strong>

What happens if this decision is wrong?

</div>


<div class="decision-item">

<strong>Reversibility</strong>

Can I test this before committing fully?

</div>


<div class="decision-item">

<strong>Opportunity Cost</strong>

What am I giving up by choosing this?

</div>


<div class="decision-item">

<strong>Next Experiment</strong>

What is the smallest useful test I can run?

</div>


</div>

</div>

</section>


</div>


</body>

</html>
